==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined from [[tetra-]] (as all of the game's pieces contain four segments) + [[tennis]].

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper-noun|-}}

# {{context|video games|trademarks}} A puzzle [[video game]] in which [[falling]] [[tetromino]]es must be manipulated to form complete lines.
# {{context|by extension}} Clearing 4 lines at once in ''Tetris''.

====Quotations====
* '''2005''': Jack Leonard, ''Bad Altitude''
*: ''While I worked out a '''''Tetris'''''-like arrangement to get all of the leftovers into the oven, Phil's curiosity got the better of him.''

